course: dictionary
lesson: 8919
title: Sideways: a word of direction
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sideways means to the side, or from the side. A crab walks sideways across the sand, moving one side first. «Turn sideways to fit through the gap» tells you to turn your body so it is narrow, not facing the gap.
explain: Sideways can also describe how you look at something. A «sideways glance» is a look without turning your head, often done secretly. The word tells you how the look was done, so picture the movement in the sentence.
explain: Use the clues around the word. In «an arch pushes the weight sideways and down into the ground», the words "down into the ground" show that sideways means a push to the side, not up. Swap your meaning in: "pushes the weight to the side" still makes sense, so you have it.
fact: Sideways means to the side, or from the side.
fact: «Sideways» can be an adverb, as in «The crab moved sideways», or an adjective, as in «a sideways look».
fact: A «sideways glance» means looking without turning your head, often secretly.
fact: In maths, a shape moved sideways has moved left or right, not up or down.
fact: Before you cross a road, look sideways, left and right, to check for traffic.
exercise: «Sifakas bounce sideways with their arms up, like dancers.» Where do the sifakas move? | Under the ground | Straight backwards into the water | *To the side, one side first | Up into the trees
exercise: «A frightened cat stands sideways and fluffs out its fur.» Why does the cat stand sideways? | To go to sleep | To catch a fish | *To look bigger | To say hello to a friend
exercise: In a maths lesson, a square is moved sideways. Which way has it moved? | Round and round in a circle | Down into the ground | *Left or right | Up into the air
test: In «Crabs famously walk sideways», what does sideways mean? | *Moving to the side, one side first | Standing still and quiet | Walking very fast in a straight line | Flying high above the sand
test: Which sentence uses sideways to mean from the side? | *She gave him a sideways glance from the corner of her eye | The lemurs leap between the trees | The arch was built a long time ago | A honeybee's sting is scraped out sideways
exam: Jayden reads «stood sideways» and thinks it means lying down. What should he do? | Skip the sentence and never read it again | Read the word aloud very quickly until it makes sense | Decide it means lying down because he guessed | *Swap in "stood to the side" and check it fits the sentence, then look sideways up if still unsure
